1. TCP vs UDP ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)
TCP is a reliable protocol. It checks whether all data reaches the destination correctly.

UDP (User Datagram Protocol)
UDP is a fast protocol. It sends data without checking whether every packet reaches the destination.

Real-Life Example

TCP
Sending money through online banking.
Every detail must reach correctly.

UDP
Video call.
If one frame is lost, the call still continues.

Difference
TCP   	UDP
Reliable	Fast
Connection-Oriented  	Connectionless
Uses ACK	     No ACK
Data arrives in order	   Order not guaranteed
Banking, Email   	Gaming, Streaming
Interview Answer
TCP is a reliable protocol that guarantees data delivery, whereas UDP is a faster protocol that does not guarantee delivery.

MCQ Facts
TCP → Reliable
UDP → Fast
TCP → Three-Way Handshake
UDP → No Handshake

