2. Hub vs Switch ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
Hub
Hub sends data to every connected device.

Switch
Switch sends data only to the correct device using the destination MAC address.

Example

4 computers are connected.

PC A wants to send data to PC C.

Hub:

A → Hub → B ❌
         → C ✅
         → D ❌

Switch:

A → Switch → C ✅
Difference
Hub	Switch
Layer 1	Layer 2
Sends to all	Sends to correct device
Slow	Faster
Less secure	More secure
Interview Answer

A hub broadcasts data to all devices, whereas a switch forwards data only to the intended device using MAC addresses.

MCQ Facts

Hub → Physical Layer
Switch → Data Link Layer
Switch → MAC Address
MCQ Facts
TCP → Reliable
UDP → Fast
TCP → Three-Way Handshake
UDP → No Handshake
------------------------------------
3. Switch vs Router ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
Switch
Connects devices inside the same network.

Router
Connects different networks.

Example

Home Wi-Fi
Laptop
↓
Switch
↓
Router
↓
Internet

Difference
Switch    	Router
Same Network	Different Networks
Uses MAC   	Uses IP
Layer 2	   Layer 3
Interview Answer

A switch connects devices within a LAN using MAC addresses, while a router connects different networks using IP addresses.

MCQ Facts

Switch → MAC

Router → IP
