4. Router vs Gateway
Simple Definition
Router

Finds the best path between networks.

Gateway

Acts as the entry or exit point of a network and can also translate between different protocols or systems.

Example

Internet

↓

Gateway

↓

Company Network

Difference
Router	Gateway
Connects Networks	Entry/Exit Point; may translate protocols
Uses Routing	Can translate between different systems/protocols
Interview Answer

A router forwards packets between networks, while a gateway connects different networks or systems and can translate between different communication protocols.
