7. IPv4 vs IPv6 ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
IPv4

Old version.

32-bit address.

IPv6

New version.

128-bit address.

Difference
IPv4	IPv6
32 bits	128 bits
Limited addresses	Huge number of addresses
Older	Newer
Interview Answer

IPv4 is a 32-bit addressing scheme, while IPv6 is a 128-bit addressing scheme introduced to overcome IPv4 address exhaustion.

MCQ Facts

IPv4 → 32 Bits

IPv6 → 128 Bits
