8. MAC vs IP ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition

MAC Address
Identifies a device on the local network.

IP Address
Identifies where the device is on a network.

Difference
MAC	IP
Physical Address	Logical Address
Layer 2	Layer 3
Switch Uses	Router Uses
Interview Answer

A MAC address identifies a device on the local network, while an IP address identifies the device's location for communication across networks.
