11. Cookies vs Sessions
Simple Definition
Cookies

Stored in the browser.

Sessions

Stored on the server.

Example

Login to Gmail.

Cookies remember your login in the browser.

The server maintains the session while you're logged in.

Difference
Cookies	Sessions
Browser	Server
Less Secure	More Secure
Can persist after browser closes	Usually ends after logout or timeout
