Cookies store user information on the browser, while sessions store user information on the server.
12. Client-Server vs Peer-to-Peer
Simple Definition
Client-Server

One server provides services.

Peer-to-Peer

Every computer can both send and receive data.

Difference
Client-Server	Peer-to-Peer
Central Server	No Central Server
Easy Management	Harder Management
Interview Answer

In the client-server model, clients communicate with a central server. In peer-to-peer, devices communicate directly with each other.

13. OSI vs TCP/IP ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
OSI

Learning model.

7 Layers.

TCP/IP

Practical model.

4 Layers.

Difference
OSI	TCP/IP
7 Layers	4 Layers
Reference Model	Internet Model
Interview Answer

