14. Packet vs Frame ⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
Packet

Data at the Network Layer.

Uses IP Address.

Frame

Data at the Data Link Layer.

Uses MAC Address.

Difference
Packet	Frame
Layer 3	Layer 2
IP Address	MAC Address
Interview Answer

A packet is the data unit of the Network Layer, while a frame is the data unit of the Data Link Layer.

15. Bandwidth vs Throughput ⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
Bandwidth

Maximum capacity of the network.

Throughput

Actual speed achieved.

Example

Internet Plan

100 Mbps

Actual Download

80 Mbps

Bandwidth = 100

Throughput = 80

Difference
Bandwidth	Throughput
Maximum Capacity	Actual Speed
Theoretical	Practical
Interview Answer

Bandwidth is the maximum capacity of a network, while throughput is the actual amount of data successfully transferred.

16. Flow Control vs Congestion Control ⭐⭐⭐⭐
Simple Definition
Flow Control

Protects the receiver from receiving data faster than it can process.

Congestion Control

Protects the network from too much traffic.

Example

Flow Control:
A fast sender sends data to a slow receiver, so the sender slows down.

Congestion Control:
Many users send data at the same time, causing traffic on the network. The sending rate is reduced to avoid overload.

Difference
Flow Control	Congestion Control
Protects Receiver	Protects Network
Between Sender & Receiver	Across the Whole Network
Interview Answer

Flow control prevents the sender from overwhelming the receiver, whereas congestion control prevents excessive traffic from overloading the network.
